          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Coinduction is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/corecursion"} corecursion
          %p
            It is a method of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            which relies on the fact that any two states of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+coalgebra"} terminal coalgebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+an+endofunctor"} for an endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            must be equal if they are indistinguishable under repeated operations of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+objects"} quotient objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimulation"} bisimulation
            between states of terminal coalgebra, that is a relation between states, such that when the coalgebra function is applied, the respective outputs are still related. Since any bisimulation must be contained within the identity relation, we can then conclude that the states are equal.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\mathbb{N}}
              be the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conatural+numbers"} conatural numbers
              and take
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi add
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mover
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ×
                      %mover
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mover
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ×
                      %mover
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} add\colon \bar{\mathbb{N}} \times \bar{\mathbb{N}} \to 1 + \bar{\mathbb{N}} \times \bar{\mathbb{N}}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n + m)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi m
                      %mo +
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m + n)
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "http://homepages.cwi.nl/~janr/papers/files-of-papers/universal_coalgebra.pdf"} Universal coalgebra: a theory of systems
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Many theorems of calculus involving formal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = \sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{a_n x^n}{n!}
              are naturally viewed as proofs by coinduction. The collection of power series
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[ [x] ]
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              (say of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              %em stream coalgebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^\mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+coalgebra+of+the+endofunctor"} terminal coalgebra of the endofunctor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Set
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \times -:\; Set \to Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %msub
                              %mi eval
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mi D
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi d
                                %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                            %mo :
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi k
                            %mo ×
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo ≥
                                %mn 0
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi a
                                  %mi n
                                %msup
                                  %mi x
                                  %mi n
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo !
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo ≥
                                %mn 0
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi a
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                                %msup
                                  %mi x
                                  %mi n
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo !
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\langle eval_0, D = \frac{d}{d x} \rangle: k[ [x] ] &amp; \to &amp; k \times k[ [x] ] \\
                    \\sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{a_n x^n}{n!} &amp; \mapsto &amp; (a_0, \sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{a_{n+1} x^n}{n!})
                    }
            %p
              Thus if we set up a bisimulation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
              between two power series
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(0) = g(0)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D f) \sim (D g)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
              (else,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[ [x] ]/\sim
              would be a proper quotient).
            %p
              As an illustration: consider a field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              of characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              and, for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 + x)^r
              to be the power series expansion of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(r \cdot \log(1 + x))
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(x) = \sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{x^n}{n!}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi log
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log(1 + x) = \sum_{n \geq 1} (-1)^{n+1}\; \frac{x^n}{n}
              is the inverse of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(x)-1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binomial+theorem"} binomial theorem
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi r
                          %munder
                            %mi k
                            %mo ̲
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 + x)^r = f(r) \coloneqq \sum_{k \geq 0} \frac{r^\underline{k} x^k}{k!}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %munder
                        %mi k
                        %mo ̲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^\underline{k}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/falling+factorial"} falling power
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r(r-1)\ldots (r-k+1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi r
                          %munder
                            %mi k
                            %mo ̲
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo !
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi log
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{k \geq 0} \frac{r^\underline{k} x^k}{k!}\; \sim\; \exp(r \cdot \log(1 + x))
            %p
              and observe first that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+coefficients"} constant coefficients
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1+x)^r
              are both
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi r
                            %munder
                              %mi k
                              %mo ̲
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo !
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mi r
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi r
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %munder
                            %mi k
                            %mo ̲
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\left(\sum_{k \geq 0} \frac{r^\underline{k} x^k}{k!}\right) = r \sum_{k \geq 0} \frac{(r-1)^\underline{k} x^k}{k!}
            %p
              (because
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %munder
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ̲
                      %mo =
                      %mi r
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %munder
                          %mi k
                          %mo ̲
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^{\underline{k+1}} = r \cdot (r-1)^{\underline{k}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi log
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\left(\exp(r \cdot \log(1 + x))\right) = r \cdot \exp((r-1) \cdot \log(1 + x))
            %p
              by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+rule"} chain rule
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(f/r) \sim D((1+x)^r/r)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f/r
              is bisimilar to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1+x)^r/r
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = (1+x)^r
